# AI News Automation & LinkedIn Publishing System — n8n Workflow

## Workflow Overview

This **n8n workflow** automatically discovers and publishes AI-related news on a scheduled basis.

It combines web scraping, AI-powered content generation, structured output parsing, social media publishing, Google Sheets logging, and AI-generated visual content into a single automated pipeline.

The workflow uses an **OpenAI-powered AI Agent** to identify and summarize relevant AI news, publishes the resulting post to **LinkedIn**, and records the publication details in **Google Sheets**.

Additionally, a secondary AI Agent generates a custom visual prompt, which is sent to **Hugging Face's FLUX.1** image-generation model to create a matching infographic.

---

## Step-by-Step Breakdown

### 1. Trigger & Data Fetching

#### Schedule Trigger

The workflow starts automatically using a **Schedule Trigger**.

* Runs on a recurring schedule.
* Current configuration: **Every 3 days**.
* Eliminates the need for manual execution.

#### HTTP Request

The workflow then uses an **HTTP Request** node to fetch raw HTML/content from:

* `ainews.com`

The retrieved content becomes the input for the AI-powered news extraction stage.

```text id="m7c2qa"
          Schedule Trigger
                │
                ▼
          HTTP Request
                │
                ▼
         ainews.com Content
                │
                ▼
            AI Agent
```

---

## 2. Main AI Processing & News Extraction

The main **AI Agent** processes the retrieved news content and prepares the LinkedIn post.

### OpenAI Chat Model — GPT-4.1-mini

The AI Agent uses **GPT-4.1-mini** as its underlying language model.

Its responsibilities include:

1. Analyzing the fetched AI news content.
2. Identifying the **top 3 relevant articles**.
3. Randomly selecting one article from the selected articles.
4. Extracting the key information from the selected article.
5. Generating a concise and engaging LinkedIn post.

### Structured Output Parser

A **Structured Output Parser** ensures that the AI Agent returns the generated information in a predefined structure.

The output includes:

* Article title
* Article link
* Summary
* Publish date
* LinkedIn post content
* Hashtags
* Emojis

The generated LinkedIn content is constrained to **under 150 words** to maintain a concise social-media format.

```text id="2l8nwp"
       AI News Content
              │
              ▼
          AI Agent
       (GPT-4.1-mini)
              │
              ├── Identify Top 3 Articles
              │
              ├── Select One Article
              │
              └── Generate LinkedIn Post
                       │
                       ▼
            Structured Output Parser
                       │
                       ▼
              Structured JSON Output
```

---

## 3. Publishing & Logging Outputs

Once the content has been generated and structured, the workflow sends the results to multiple destinations.

### Google Sheets

The workflow automatically appends the generated content to a designated Google Sheets document:

* **Sheet:** `linkedin posts`

The sheet acts as a tracking and logging layer for generated publications.

It can store information such as:

* Article title
* Article URL
* Generated summary
* LinkedIn post
* Publish date
* Other structured output fields

### LinkedIn

The selected article is published directly to an **organization's LinkedIn page**.

The published content includes:

* Article title
* AI-generated summary
* Hashtags
* Emojis

This allows the workflow to operate as an automated **AI news publishing pipeline** without requiring manual content creation for each post.

---

## 4. Infographic Generation Sub-Pipeline

In parallel with the publishing and logging process, the workflow generates a custom visual for the selected news article.

### AI Agent1 — Visual Prompt Generation

**AI Agent1** receives the generated news/post content and converts it into a specialized prompt for image generation.

The prompt is designed specifically to produce an **infographic-style visual** that matches the topic of the selected AI news article.

The generated prompt can describe elements such as:

* Main subject
* Key concepts
* Visual hierarchy
* Infographic composition
* Relevant technology concepts
* Professional visual style
* Supporting graphical elements

```text id="9d4xkt"
       Generated News Content
                │
                ▼
            AI Agent1
                │
                ▼
       Infographic Prompt
                │
                ▼
         HTTP Request1
                │
                ▼
       Hugging Face API
                │
                ▼
      FLUX.1-schnell Model
                │
                ▼
          PNG Image
```

### HTTP Request1 — Hugging Face Image Generation

The generated image prompt is sent through an **HTTP POST request** to the Hugging Face inference API.

The workflow uses the following model:

```text id="e5q2rx"
black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-schnell
```

The model generates a custom **PNG image** based on the AI-generated infographic prompt.

